WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.880
As you might know, Dwayne Johnson is a Hollywood
mainstay with so many famous movie credits

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.700
to his name that it's easy to lose count of
them all.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.691
Ever since he made his transition from being
The Rock in the WWE to the big screen, Johnson

00:00:12.691 --> 00:00:17.261
has joined a number of ongoing franchises,
but there is one franchise for which he is

00:00:17.261 --> 00:00:20.440
very well known — "The Fast and the Furious."

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:25.250
Since first appearing as Hobbs in "Fast Five"
back in 2011, Johnson went on to reprise the

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.250
role four more times, including in the spin-off
film in which he co-stars with Jason Statham,

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.770
"Fast &amp; Furious Presents: Hobbs &amp; Shaw."

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:37.170
However, the only thing more well-known about
Johnson playing Hobbs — other than him kicking

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:42.500
butt and taking names — is the notorious
beef between Johnson and Mr. Family himself,

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:43.500
Vin Diesel.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.540
Diesel, of course, has played Dominic Toretto
in the "Fast &amp; Furious" franchise from the

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:53.070
very beginning and continues to star in the
franchise's films, including the latest installment,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.070
"F9."

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:59.489
As big of a star as The Rock may be, Vin Diesel
is basically the face of the "Fast &amp; Furious"

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:04.610
franchise, so this latest unfortunate development
wasn't exactly unforeseeable — especially

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:06.990
in light of said public beef.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:11.380
Johnson did not appear in "F9," and now he
has something to say about both that omission

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.920
and whether or not he'll appear in any other
films within the franchise going forward.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.850
Two things of note are worth mentioning before
discussing Dwayne Johnson's future in the

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.650
"Fast &amp; Furious" movie franchise.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:26.560
One, there are supposedly only two more movies
left in the franchise before the story wraps.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.249
Two, Vin Diesel recently tried to explain
the feud between him and Dwayne Johnson.

00:01:31.249 --> 00:01:35.709
In a recent interview with Men's Health, Diesel
passed off the beef as intentional on his

00:01:35.709 --> 00:01:36.709
part.

00:01:36.709 --> 00:01:37.709
Diesel said,

00:01:37.709 --> 00:01:39.259
"I could give a lot of tough love.

00:01:39.259 --> 00:01:43.169
Not Felliniesque, but I would do anything
I'd have to do in order to get performances

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.849
in anything I'm producing."

00:01:44.849 --> 00:01:49.040
While doing an interview alongside Emily Blunt
with The Hollywood Reporter to promote "Jungle

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.709
Cruise," their upcoming Disney film, Johnson
responded bluntly:

00:01:52.709 --> 00:01:55.930
"I laughed and I laughed hard.I think everyone
had a laugh at that.

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.409
And I'll leave it at that."

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:00.319
And by “leave it at that” he meant, “expand
on the situation….”

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:01.860
"And that I've wished them well.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.310
I wish them well on '[F9].'

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:08.299
And I wish them the best of luck on 'Fast
10' and 'Fast 11' and the rest of the 'Fast

00:02:08.299 --> 00:02:10.720
&amp; Furious' movies they do that will be without
me."

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:15.110
In other words, it certainly seems like Johnson
is done with "The Fast &amp; Furious" franchise

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.110
permanently.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.340
Emily Blunt sarcastically chimed in about
Diesel, saying,

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.930
"Just thank God he was there.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:21.930
[...] Thank God.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.390
He carried you through that."

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.750
"Felliniesque," Johnson said in response.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:30.000
Just so we’re clear — Felliniesque would
refer to the famous Italian director who created

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.180
bizarre, abstract films, — that were more
like works of art.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.870
You know, just like the Fast Franchise, right?

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:40.750
There was plenty of space in Diesel's somewhat
self-serving explanation of the beef for Johnson

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:45.410
to leave it squashed, but his comments during
the press junket for "Jungle Cruise" suggest

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:48.020
hatchet burying isn't in the cards for him
and Vin.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:52.440
While he never provided anything close to
the Full Sherman in his response to questions

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.010
about his future with the "Fast &amp; Furious"
franchise, his obvious disdain for Diesel's

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:01.340
comments — not to mention the sarcastic
addition from Blunt — suggest it would take

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:04.230
quite an overture to rope him back into the
family.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.030
It's not like he's really hurting for the
work, either.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:10.950
Johnson just completed what he described as
one of the most physically and mentally demanding

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:16.210
experiences of his career preparing for and
filming "Black Adam," and given the anticipation

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:20.790
for that particular feature, it seems likely
he'll become a mainstay with the DC Extended

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.240
Universe for the foreseeable future.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:28.120
Long before that superhero flick reaches screens,
however, his starring turn in the long-awaited

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.290
"Jungle Cruise" is set to debut.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:34.720
The House of Mouse certainly hopes that "Jungle
Cruise" will become the next "Pirates of the

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.480
Caribbean," in which case Dwayne Johnson's
Frank "Skipper" Wolff will be the next Captain

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.730
Jack Sparrow.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:42.560
That sounds like another franchise role if
we've ever heard one.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:48.140
"Jungle Cruise" hits theaters on Friday, July
30th and will also be available on Disney+

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.040
Premier Access for $29.99.

